WEBVTT

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.320
PEDESTRIANS AND BICYCLES ONLY

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.670
2017, fall.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.050
NURSE STATION
PATIENT ROOMS

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:02.270
My uncle was struck by a truck
when he was 17.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.850
After 17 years of being in a coma…

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.440
he awoke.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:26.250
Irellars Granbahamal tona galtoeba rilex.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.340
He had gone insane.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.970
Yes, well…

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.260
Japanese?

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:41.970
Sorry about that.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.980
I just came back from spending
17 years in Granbahamal.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.900
Let's check your temperature.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.280
Zalbe madira kolstonam kolstonam.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.660
Isn't that right?

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:05.290
Del storba tona rabelt gal.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.040
All right, see you during the next round.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.680
You must be Takafumi, my sister's kid.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.260
You've grown up.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.600
Where is everyone?

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.480
After you fell into a coma,

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:33.440
the family fought bitterly over
what to do with you until it fell apart.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.610
Honestly speaking,
my mom would rather not see you.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.570
MY FAMILY FELL APART
DUE TO FIGHTING OVER ME

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.280
Icuras cuora.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:48.870
Well then,

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.080
let me prove to you that
I lived in another world.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.460
What? No, thanks.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.260
War-grent seld.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.130
SPRING WATER

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:01.720
What?

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.600
War-grent magna!

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.890
War-grent rald!

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.730
-This is hard to watch…
-War-grent neld!

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.810
War-grent gad!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:13.900
War-grent pad!

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.820
-You know…
-War-grent larch!

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.280
…the economic decline
has been hard on me, too.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.110
I work part-time to support myself.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.950
I brought papers for you to apply
for self-reliance support and whatnot.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.280
Wind, lift!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.000
No way!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.920
Wind, return.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.340
Japanese works in this world.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.610
It's true.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:06.030
Anyway, were you about to hit me
with harsh reality just now?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.490
-Nope.
-You sure?

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:09.910
What did you do just now?

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.370
Magic.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.040
Fire.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.630
That's amazing! How do you do that?

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.960
Never mind it.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.630
Who's winning the Console War? Is it SEGA?

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:22.760
What?

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.590
SEGA? Nowadays?

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:30.600
In Japan, Sony and Nintendo
dominate the industry.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.350
What? What about SEGA?

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.140
-Is that something you need to know--
-What about SEGA?

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:39.110
Well… it gave up making consoles
a good while ago.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.450
Icuras cuora.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.370
What does "icuras cuora" do?

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.160
This spell erases memories.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.420
I use it when things get unbearable.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.250
Is SEGA's decline such a big shock to him?

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.250
The other world was fraught
with difficulties.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.710
Want to take a look?

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.220
Oh, sure.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:18.350
Make me forget everything I read just now.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.400
I told you.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.740
Spirits of memory, deliver unto oblivion.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.780
SEGA's decline
truly was heart-wrenching to him.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.330
One week later…

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:37.210
I decided to make a living
by making money off of my uncle's powers.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.170
ANOTHER WORLD - LIGHTSABER

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:40.920
I uploaded videos on YouTube

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.710
and earned about 60,000 yen from ads.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.220
UNCLE:
YOU'RE FINE THE WAY YOU ARE

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.130
GET HOME

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.390
SOLD CHEAPER THAN A SCOURING PAD

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.990
I shouldn't say this, since I'm crashing,
but isn't this unit too big for just you?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.250
Yeah, I used to share this room
with someone else,

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.500
but I had troubles with them.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.500
A roommate? Was it a girlfriend?

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:44.920
Well, no…

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.040
Wow…

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:49.460
No, it's called a room share!
Haven't you heard of it?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.510
No.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.010
HISTORY OF ROOM SHARE

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:54.890
There was no such thing 17 years ago?

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.560
Wow, you looked that up in seconds.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.810
Electronic dictionaries sure have evolved.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.600
Yep… Wait, what?

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.060
Little Takafumi…

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.900
is old enough to recruit friends
and live with them.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.660
What were your friends like
in the other world?

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.920
I basically played solo for 17 years.

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:34.720
Is that right…

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.440
Everyone over there is good-looking.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.900
They're all handsome men
and beautiful women.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.860
That's great.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.440
I must have looked ugly…

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.750
I was hunted down as an orc variant.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.830
Uncle, hold on.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.710
-Then--
-It's too heavy!

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.920
I don't want to hear this
while washing the dishes.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:18.090
That's how it usually went,
but some were particularly aggressive.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:19.680
I told you to wait!

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:23.180
They followed me around every day
and pestered and harassed me.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:27.190
No matter what I did, they made fun of me
and wouldn't let me be who I am.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.230
How horrible…

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.110
So that's the reality
of a parallel world fantasy life.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:39.570
I saved her life when I met her.
She didn't even thank me.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.490
She sounds like the worst.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.740
Right?

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:47.580
She said, "No one asked for your help.
Don't touch me!

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.540
Don't misinterpret it.
I didn't save you for your sake.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:57.260
I must be the only one who can stand
being with an orc face like you!"

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:01.430
She berated me to no end.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.720
I got rid of her in some city
and took off.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.150
Don't touch me!

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:13.900
Don't misinterpret me!

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.740
I must be the only one who can stand
being with an orc face like you.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:30.210
The concept of tsundere
became popular around 2004.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.920
Four years after my uncle left
for the other world.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.210
What happened to her afterwards?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.130
What? Who knows?

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:45.390
Anyway, my life didn't go well
in the other world, either.

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:49.060
But now I've come back,

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.310
there's the Internet, optical fiber,
and even "wii-fii"!

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:54.230
This is great!

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.690
With videos, even I can connect
with people from around the world.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.150
What?

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.740
EVEN A 5TH GRADER LIKE ME
CAN TELL HOW FAKE THIS IS.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:03.120
SUCH AMATEUR EDITING.
IS IT A BAD JOKE?

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.700
My uncle,
who returned from the other world…

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:08.870
LOLOL -
MAD FACE UNCLE

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:11.120
…stepped into a brand-new world,
the Internet.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.500
What? How can they see my face?

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.210
-Maybe through this tiny lens?
-It's what people say on the Internet.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.300
A "sock puppet"? I'm not a hoax!

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.800
Those are commonly used phrases.
Nothing more.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:27.180
Hey, why is "LOL" everywhere?

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:30.430
He doesn't know how to deal with
haters yet.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.940
MEMORY INTO OBLIVION - THANKS

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:35.020
USED - GOOD

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.150
I want this cell phone.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.900
It doesn't open up but slides around.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.950
Uncle, that one's a 2G.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.280
Can I buy it through this online auction?

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:47.790
You can't make calls on it
since it uses an outdated radio wave.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.250
That's fine. I don't care about calls.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.330
What about your junior high
and high school friends?

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:55.580
Takafumi,

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:02.170
a man who chooses SEGA console
cannot live an ordinary life.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.260
PERSONAL OPINION

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:09.560
Why do game consoles dictate
so much of his life?

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.810
That one looks like the cheapest option.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.520
You already researched it.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.650
Those smartphones may be tiny,
but they sure are powerful.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.190
You'll soon get the hang of it.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:26.410
"Touch," "swipe," "pinch out"…

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:29.870
For now,
I want a phone with lots of buttons.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:30.950
Yeah?

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:36.790
But the cool ones that open up,
slide, or spin around are all gone.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:39.920
Technological innovation.
Everyone uses touch panel phones now.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.920
That's 17 years of innovation.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:47.090
Actually, I made a technological
advancement in the other world.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.930
What did you invent?

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:53.730
I created a vase that poured out water
in a drought-stricken village.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.480
Awesome! How did you do that?

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.020
I used two spells to…

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:01.320
It'll be easier to show you my memory.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:02.690
Icuras elran.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.620
This image!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:12.080
It's your memory from the other world!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.750
These magic-storing cards
are called talismans.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:21.880
I'll forgo the details, but it worked by
reversing the water electrolysis process.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.170
Modern science is undefeated!

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.180
Uncle, you dominated the other world.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:31.100
The people must have sung your praises
and revered you.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:32.600
Not really.

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:38.440
They tried to hang me.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.440
The vase, smashed to smithereens.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:49.200
It wasn't acceptable in their religion.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:50.780
Hold it!

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.870
Someone came to rescue you.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:56.210
Yeah, that's the girl
bent on harassing me.

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:57.920
This girl?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:02.170
Yes, he has an evil countenance.
He is more like an orc than a man.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:04.960
I don't blame you for distrusting him,
however--

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:06.510
War-grent grakka.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.640
That was rough…

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.100
That's how it went.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:20.980
Sorry.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:24.650
It's hard to see
from the first-person view.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.730
That bothers you?

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:30.610
Swipe it like this to turn the camera.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.580
-Here we go.
-How is that possible?

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.080
Pinch in to make it smaller.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.710
They almost hunted you down.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:41.040
Can we see what happened to that girl?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:44.250
Sure. Let's pinch out to enlarge.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.090
There she is.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:50.380
That coward…

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.510
He ran away.

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:58.430
Goodness…

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:01.690
What a kind girl!
She's also super beautiful!

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.440
That's right, I'm a coward.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.530
END OF AUCTION NOTIFICATION

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:07.740
Yes, the auction.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:08.650
TIME LEFT

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.570
It's about to end!

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.870
PLACE A BID

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.080
I'm placing a bid!

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:16.580
What's the shipping cost?

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:17.790
What?

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.040
AUCTION ENDED -
CONGRATULATIONS! YOU WON!

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.120
CHECK YOUR TRANSACTION

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.420
BID WON - 1,600 YEN,
SHIPMENT FEE - 2,000 YEN

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.340
The shipping is 2,000 yen.

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.880
It's shipped from a remote island
I've never heard of.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:35.260
We don't have to pay for shipping
if we pick it up in person.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:49.900
What?

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:53.360
Uncle!

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.160
I'll be back soon.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.250
30 MINUTES LATER

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:08.340
I'm back.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:14.260
Uncle…

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:19.010
How do you like this headphone?

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:21.350
-Where is it auctioned from?
-Kumamoto.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.440
Five minutes tops.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:26.900
How about this couch?

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.570
Too heavy to haul around.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.530
I'll give you a shoulder massage
afterward.

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:32.440
Well, okay then.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.990
My uncle learned how to buy online
with free shipping.

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:40.540
Thank you.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:44.830
I could have gone to get it.

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:47.000
This rice was on a special discount
on Amazon.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:48.210
Can you grab me a knife?

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:52.260
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.800
What's this? Where'd you get it?

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:58.640
Dimensional storage.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.640
Also, this. It's for slaying dragons,
so handle with caution.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.890
You had that at the hospital.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:06.980
Do you have anything else
from the other world?

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:08.110
Certainly.

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.480
I have this magic sword.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:15.150
My deposit…

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.320
I have precious metals, too.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:21.410
This crystallization of mermaid's tears
was crafted with magic.

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:24.000
This ring is sculpted from rainbow coral.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.790
This gem alone can pay to build a castle
in the other world.

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:28.080
Let's sell it!

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:30.340
Fifty yen.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.300
I took it to a pawn shop.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:35.420
It was appraised for 50 yen.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:36.760
It's a bit too rare.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:41.560
Our views aren't growing.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:43.520
We need a breakthrough.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:44.680
Uncle,

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:49.400
did you have this ring because
you meant to gift it to someone?

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.780
Not really.
Gems are more like memorabilia.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:56.610
They can only be obtained
after beating challenging dungeons.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:57.860
Is that so?

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:09.000
You want to talk about relationships?

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:13.170
Not really. You don't seem interested in
that kind of thing. So, no thanks.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:16.510
Cut the nonsense.
I've lived for over 30 years.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:18.090
That comes with experience.

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:23.100
I met my first love in grade school.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.390
What were they like?

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.230
They were Sonic and Tails.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.060
What?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:41.240
I stopped by the toy shop's display window
every day and spent hours watching the TV.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:47.120
The title scene was so cute,
I never got tired of it.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.330
Do you have any experience
involving people?

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:50.830
Of course I do.

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:54.800
Kaede Nanase was a good friend of mine.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.970
The enemy group's leader murdered her.

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.680
She was then revived as a living machine.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:04.390
They relentlessly attack her to obtain
the salvation weapon Seven Force.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.680
Stage three's boss is the fifth form of…

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:10.310
Does he have any experience
outside of video games in his life?

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:13.230
Did you meet any girls in the other world?

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.190
-I did.
-What?

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:18.650
Icuras elran.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.630
Thank you very much.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:15.080
And that's how I saved her from a monster.

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:19.590
More like she offered her life
in exchange for her brothers'.

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:21.470
Wasn't that smooth?

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:25.510
Immediately afterward, I was struck
from a blind spot by some goblins.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:28.760
They threw me off a cliff,
and that was that.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:30.640
What a disaster.

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:37.480
The two brothers snuck behind him
with terrifying looks on their faces.

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:39.860
Let's check how that ambush occurred.

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.400
I'm sure they were goblins.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:44.110
-Yeah?
-Yeah, absolutely!

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:49.410
I was on the brink of death
when she stumbled into me.

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:52.290
I hate to say this, but she saved me.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:05.340
You…

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:07.890
Why did you…

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:09.180
Don't you misunderstand.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:11.060
You are indebted to me now.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:14.140
Spend the rest of your life bowing to me.

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:17.230
The rest of my life?

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:18.310
What?

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.940
That's not what I meant.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.530
I didn't mean "together forever"
or anything.

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:30.120
W-what? Stay away from me!

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.040
I'd rather not owe you a huge favor.

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:34.830
-Will this do?
-What?

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.000
What?

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:41.840
It's a cosmite ring, said to be
one of the only seven in existence.

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:44.340
What are you doing?

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:50.760
How does it fit?

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:52.810
Wait, hold on!

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.140
It's too sudden…

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:57.520
Do you not want it?

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:05.360
I do…

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:14.870
My uncle is about to do
something outrageous!

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:17.250
Was that okay to do?

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:21.840
Looks like it means the same in the other
world. Did you take responsibility?

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:23.170
Of course I did.

00:22:25.420 --> 00:22:28.630
I was responsible enough to have it
redeemed at the next town.

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:30.220
Uncle!

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:40.400
You said you dodged her in some town.
So it was this one.

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:42.900
No. She kept following me around.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.780
Maybe she got a taste for money.

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:48.200
I deposited it at a bank.
Where are you going next?

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:51.570
What? You'll stay here for now?
What a coincidence. Me, too!

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.120
She's resilient.

00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:56.200
As you can see,

00:22:56.290 --> 00:22:59.710
these kinds of rare items
can be useful on many occasions.

00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:02.920
Let's stash that knife in here.

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.040
Sure.

00:23:15.140 --> 00:23:16.470
UNCLE!?

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:20.310
My uncle's new video
surpassed 2,000,000 views.

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:22.850
I'M ALIVE

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:40.000
2017, fall.

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:42.960
My new life with my uncle

00:23:44.380 --> 00:23:46.250
had just begun.

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:50.920
Subtitle translation by:
Minoru Nishikawa
